\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My Saviour, Thou Thy love to me
\par In shame, in want, in pain hast showed;
\par For me, on the accursed tree,
\par Thou pouredst forth Thy guiltless blood;
\par Thy wounds upon my heart impress,
\par Nor aught shall the loved stamp efface.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. More hard than marble is my heart,
\par And foul with sins of deepest stain;
\par But Thou the mighty Saviour art,
\par Nor flowed Thy cleansing blood in vain:
\par Ah, soften, melt this rock, and may
\par Thy blood wash all these stains away!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O that I, as a little child,
\par May follow Thee, and never rest
\par Till sweetly Thou hast breathed Thy mild
\par And lowly mind into my breast!
\par Nor ever may we parted be,
\par Till I become one spirit with Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Still let Thy love point out my way;
\par How wondrous  things Thy love hath wrought!
\par Still lead me, lest i go astray;
\par Direct my word, inspire my thought;
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

